# Civil War Strategy: the Union's fleet meets the Rebel fleet, retreats, raids and sails back,
# and a Union army beats the army in Richmond. The game is loaded from a prepared save
# (tests/data/navy-fights/cws1.save): May 1862, the Union plays, its fleet led by an ironclad;
# the Rebel fleet lies in Mobile. The computer is passive. The map starts with city names but
# not the full pictures (graf=2).
#! seed 1862
#! cfg bold=0 graf=2 history=1
#! data navy-fights
#! files cws.his

rule 1 key space
rule 2:E text y
rule 2:R key enter

# The title menu: Resume Saved Game; the Load menu: the one save.
play until 2:V
text r
play until 2:L
key enter
play until 2:M
digest

# UTILITY, End Cond. Victory Conditions starts on Time: down and Enter turn off each of the
# four others. Esc there, and Esc at the Utility menu.
text u
prompt
text e
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
prompt
key esc
prompt
key esc
prompt

# May 1862. Ships, Sail, to Mobile, where the Rebel fleet lies: the Options menu of a sea
# fight. Esc there shows it again. Retreat: the fleet goes back to Philadelphia.
text s
prompt
text s
prompt
digest
text m
prompt
digest
key esc
prompt
text r
prompt
digest

# Moves: Fremont, from Fredericksburg to Richmond, where a Rebel army stands. In the turn's
# update he wins and takes the capital, and the beaten army flees to a Rebel city.
text m
prompt
text f
prompt
text r
prompt
digest
text e

# July 1862. Ships, Raid: the fleet sails to raid commerce, without the picture of its ship.
play until 2:M
digest
text s
prompt
text r
prompt
digest
text e

# September 1862. Ships, Sail, from raiding to the first port. UTILITY, Graphics: the full map.
play until 2:M
digest
text s
prompt
text s
prompt
digest
key enter
prompt
digest
text u
prompt
text g
prompt
key esc
prompt
digest
text e

# November 1862. Ships, Raid: the fleet sails with the picture of the ironclad that leads it.
play until 2:M
digest
text s
prompt
text r
prompt
digest

# Files, Quit to DOS, Yes, and a key for END's "Press any key to continue".
text f
prompt
text q
prompt
text y
repeat space
